            "(DraftReplacement) or discontinue it (§10.3 A.1 'A mismatch returns the order to the prescriber'; SI-03 clause b)",
    ),
    RESUBMIT_FOR_VERIFICATION(
        "resubmitForVerification",
        "the verification status becomes pending again, the return task closes with the prescriber's response, and the verification task " +
            "returns to the top of the queue. Independently calculated doses recorded before the resubmission stay on record and no " +
            "longer count: the pharmacist records a fresh one (controlSetASatisfied)",
    ),
    FLAG_IF_IDENTITY_NOT_REVERIFIED(
        "flagIfIdentityNotReverified",
        "if identityReverificationSatisfied does not hold for this command (the issuing session's context changed within the window and " +
            "the issuer did not confirm a re-verification), the command still takes effect, is journaled as 'identity not re-verified', " +
            "and an owned task goes to the ordering practitioner and the patient's nurse to confirm it was meant for this patient. " +
            "Nothing otherwise (DN-052 item 2)",
    ),
    SUSPEND_FULFILMENT(
        "suspendFulfilment",
        "the order is held: its verification status is unchanged (a returned order stays returned); fulfilling modules suspend its work: " +
            "no dose of a held order is administrable (the MAR's activeVerifiedOrder and orderAwaitingVerification both need an unheld " +
            "state), its doses are not flagged late, and a dose whose late-dose window passes while the order is held closes as not-done " +
            "with the reason order-on-hold (medication-administration.yaml); pharmacy stops dispensing it; a verification task is " +
            "paused; uncollected specimens wait. The hold appears in the ordering practitioner's open-order view",
    ),
    RESUME_FULFILMENT(
        "resumeFulfilment",
        "the hold ends: the verification status is unchanged; fulfilling modules resume the order's work from the resume time; a paused " +
            "verification task returns to the queue; an open hold review task closes",
    ),
    CREATE_DRAFT_OWNER_TASK(
        "createDraftOwnerTask",
        "an owned task with an SLA goes to the draft's owner to sign or discard it: the author, or for a cutover pre-build the " +
            "prescriber it names, with the pharmacist who pre-built it informed (SI-03 clause b; §21 row 3.13)",
    ),
    CREATE_HOLD_REVIEW_TASK(
        "createHoldReviewTask",
        "an owned task with an SLA goes to the ordering practitioner to resume or discontinue the held order (SI-03 clause b)",
    ),
    LINK_REPLACING_ORDER(
        "linkReplacingOrder",
        "the revoked order records the replacing order's id (R11 §7.2 replaces), and one OrderModified event (§8.5) is journaled for the " +
            "pair; no OrderDiscontinued is published for a replacement",
    ),
    CLOSE_OPEN_FULFILMENT(
        "closeOpenFulfilment",
        "the order has ended (revoked, replaced, completed or entered in error): fulfilling modules close its open work. The MAR " +
            "receives OrderEnded for each of its scheduled and in-progress doses: it closes a scheduled dose as not-done with the reason " +
            "order-ended and raises an owned stop task for a running infusion (medication-administration.yaml). Pharmacy stops " +
            "dispensing, the lab cancels uncollected specimens, and the order leaves the open-order view. A dose already given offline " +
            "against it is kept as a fact and flagged to the prescriber and pharmacist as an owned task (§9.10 mobile offline BCMA; " +
            "SI-15; CTRL-0015-9). Nothing is left open for a completed order",
    ),
    PUBLISH_ORDER_DISCONTINUED(
        "publishOrderDiscontinued",
        "an OrderDiscontinued event (§8.5) is journaled with the reason, the issuer and the time",
    ),
    CLOSE_ORDER_TRACKING(
        "closeOrderTracking",
        "the order leaves the overdue 'not yet resulted' view; results still pending for a discharged patient stay in owned queues " +
            "(SI-17, results routing)",
    ),
    FLAG_ENTERED_IN_ERROR(
        "flagEnteredInError",
        "the order is shown as entered in error, never deleted (H6), its open work is closed (closeOpenFulfilment) and every module " +
            "holding facts derived from it (MAR entries, specimens, results, charges through the outbox) is told to flag them; the " +
            "recipients of earlier messages about the order are notified",
    ),
}

/** The guard predicates of the order machine, implemented once by the domain (OrderGuards). */
@Suppress("TooManyFunctions")
interface OrderPredicates {
    /**
     * the order is a medication order: its orderable is a formulary medicine (R11 §7.1 MedicationRequest). The kind is set when the draft
     * is created and never changes
     */
    fun medicationOrder(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the exact complement of medicationOrder: any other order kind of §9.5 (laboratory, imaging, procedures, nursing, diet, activity,
     * consults, referrals, blood products, isolation, ADT, therapy, respiratory, code status)
     */
    fun notMedicationOrder(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the command's principal is a human user who authenticated for this signature (§9.4 authentication, intent and manifestation; a Trust
     * Plane answer, WP-0.4). An AI agent, a service principal, an interface or a migration loader never signs an order (SI-07 'AI never
     * signs orders', applied before P2; DN-052 item 12). An unknown principal kind fails
     */
    fun signerAuthenticatedHuman(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the ordering practitioner (the signer; for a verbal or telephone order, the practitioner who gave it) has a practitioner licence
     * whose expiry is after the server's time of the command and holds, at this hospital, the delineated privilege that the governed
     * privilege configuration requires for this orderable (§9.26 'privilege checks gate order entry'; 'an expired licence blocks new orders
     * immediately'). A missing licence, an unknown expiry or a missing privilege fails. Used only on Sign: it never gates a stop
     */
    fun ordererPrivileged(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the issuer is a human user who holds, at this hospital, the privilege that the governed privilege configuration (§9.26, TRU-IAM-02)
     * requires for this command on this order kind, with a licence valid at the server's time of the command where that privilege needs a
     * licensed role. An unknown user, an unknown requirement or a missing privilege fails. Used on Discard, Resume and Resubmit, never on a
     * stop
     */
    fun actorPrivileged(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the issuer may hold this order (DN-052 item 14): (a) a human user who holds the hold privilege that the governed configuration names
     * for this order kind; or, when that configuration is missing or names nobody, any prescriber on the patient's care team (ADR-024) or
     * any pharmacist (hold pending clarification), a vendor-locked baseline; or (b) a system or interface principal authenticated as itself
     * and registered in governed configuration to hold orders for a system reason. The issuer's licence expiry is never checked (§9.26
     * blocks new orders, not stops). An AI agent never qualifies (SI-07). An unknown principal fails
     */
    fun mayHoldOrder(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the issuer may discontinue this order (DN-052 item 14): (a) a human user who holds the discontinue privilege that the governed
     * configuration names for this order kind; or, when that configuration is missing or names nobody, any prescriber on the patient's care
     * team (ADR-024), a vendor-locked baseline; or (b) a system or interface principal authenticated as itself and registered in governed
     * configuration to discontinue orders for a system reason (for example a death or discharge recorded by ADT). The issuer's licence
     * expiry is never checked. An AI agent never qualifies (SI-07). An unknown principal fails
     */
    fun mayDiscontinueOrder(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the issuer is a human user who holds the pharmacist verification privilege at this hospital (§9.10 MED-PHV-01; §9.26), with a
     * pharmacist licence whose expiry is after the server's time of the command
     */
    fun verifierIsPharmacist(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the verifying pharmacist is not the ordering practitioner, not the user who signed the order, not the receiver of a verbal or
     * telephone order, and not the user who created the draft (for a cutover pre-build, the pharmacist who pre-built it). DN-052 item 7
     */
    fun verifierIndependentOfOrderer(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * SI-16 'Identity is re-verified at signing if the context changed within the last 60 s', checked by the server (CTRL-0016-1,
     * CTRL-0016-7) with the readings of DN-026, DN-027 and DN-028 (DN-052 items 1 and 2). The facts are the issuing session's last
     * patient-context change time as recorded by the server-side patient context (not built: KA-025), the server's receipt time of the
     * command, the tenant's re-verification window and the latest re-verification answer the command relies on. The window is the tenant's
     * value but never less than 60 000 ms (vendor-locked: a tenant may lengthen it and never shorten it). The change is within the window
     * when the elapsed time from the change to the receipt is at most the window, inclusive (DN-026), and also when the change time is
     * unknown or the elapsed time is negative (fails closed). The predicate holds when either (a) the change is not within the window and
     * no re-verification answer recorded after the change is 'Not this patient' (DN-027: a disputed identity needs re-verification even
     * after 60 s); or (b) the latest re-verification answer recorded after the change (or, when the change time is unknown, recorded for
     * this command) is a confirmation by the user who issues this command (DN-027). A change is any change of the context's patient id,
     * including from none and to none (DN-028). The re-verification is one inline step of the sign dialog (patient-context.yaml), never a
     * second screen. Guards Sign, Verify, Resume, Resubmit and Mark error only
     */
    fun identityReverificationSatisfied(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the command was issued while the on-site cell was reachable, or in an offline mode for which the offline matrix (ADR-012,
     * CTRL-0015-3; governed data the CSO approves) lists full CDS as available; today no mode is listed, so every offline mode fails. The
     * fact is the mode in which the user issued the command (from the command's offline envelope), not the mode when a queued command
     * reaches the server: a command issued offline is refused when the server revalidates it (SI-15 'Offline commands are revalidated by
     * the server'). Losing the internet or the WAN alone leaves an on-site cell online (SI-15 last sentence); only a lost on-site cell,
     * edge-agent mode or mobile offline mode is offline. An unknown mode fails. Guards Sign and Verify only, never a stop. DN-052 item 3
     */
    fun notOfflineWithoutFullCds(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * no governed local hard-stop rule whose trigger matches this order fired in the CDS evaluation for this command (Tier A rules on the
     * governed list that run in the CDS runtime without the drug KB, for example a fatal route; the CDS registry's answer, CTRL-0014-3). A
     * rule that fired is never overridable. The runtime evaluates local rules to completion, so a latency overrun alone never counts
     * against this predicate. A matching rule that could not run (runtime error) fails closed (§9.6 'hard stops fail closed'), except for
     * an orderable on the governed emergency override list or an order with priority STAT: then the predicate holds and the check is
     * recorded as unavailable (recordCdsGaps) for the pharmacist or the ordering practitioner to review
     */
    fun localHardStopsSatisfied(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * no drug-KB dose rule fired a Tier A hard stop for this command: either the KB answered with a ratio, flag or maximum in exactly the
     * ordered unit and the governed ≥10× threshold was not met (§10.3 A.2; §2.1 clause c; CTRL-0005-10), or the KB gave no usable answer
     * (outage, error, no ratio, flag or maximum, a unit other than the ordered unit, or no answer within its time budget). No usable answer
     * never refuses: 'dose check unavailable' is recorded and shown, and the order is routed to pharmacist review (recordCdsGaps; §2.1
     * clause c; CTRL-0005-7). Holds for an order that no KB dose rule covers
     */
    fun kbHardStopNotFired(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * every interruptive (Tier B) alert that the CDS evaluation for this command raised was resolved by changing the order (which runs the
     * evaluation again) or overridden with an override reason the user chose (never defaulted, §6.5; SI-14; the channel adapter owns the
     * 'chosen' mark, and a channel that cannot supply one cannot override). A service that did not answer within its budget raised no
     * alert: it fails open with the §9.6 banner and is recorded by recordCdsGaps, never a refusal
     */
    fun interruptiveAlertsAnswered(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * every CDS check recorded as unavailable for this order (recordCdsGaps: a KB dose check, or a local hard-stop check that could not
     * run) has since answered without firing in the evaluation for this Verify, or the verifying pharmacist recorded a documented manual
     * check for it with an attestation (the control set A pattern, §10.3 A.1). Holds when no gap is recorded
     */
    fun cdsGapsReviewed(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * no governed co-sign rule (content [HUMAN]; for example a rule naming signer roles whose orders need a co-signature before they take
     * effect) requires a co-signature before activation for this signer and orderable; or that co-signature is recorded by a practitioner
     * other than the signer who satisfies ordererPrivileged's licence and privilege conditions for this orderable and authenticated for the
     * co-signature (R11 §10.2 'signed (and co-signed if required)'). Whether such a rule exempts STAT orders is part of the governed rule
     * (DN-052 item 18). The co-signature that a verbal order owes after activation is verbalOrderDocumented's, not this one
     */
    fun coSignRuleSatisfied(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the order is not a verbal or telephone order; or it is one entered in a situation the governed verbal-order policy allows (content
     * [HUMAN]; §9.5 'only in defined situations') by a receiving user who holds the privilege to receive verbal orders
     */
    fun verbalOrderPermitted(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the order is not a verbal or telephone order; or the read-back is recorded with the source practitioner, the receiving user and the
     * time (§9.5 'read-back captured with source and receiver'), and a co-sign due time is set that is after the receipt time and no later
     * than the receipt time plus the governed co-sign limit (content [HUMAN]; §8.4 'verbal orders carry read-back and a co-sign due time').
     * Time comparison only, never dose arithmetic
     */
    fun verbalOrderDocumented(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the order is not a verbal or telephone order for an orderable flagged antineoplastic in the formulary (governed content [HUMAN]; an
     * unknown flag counts as antineoplastic). §8.4 'refused for antineoplastics'; §9.5 'except hold or stop', which are Hold and
     * Discontinue, never Sign
     */
    fun notVerbalAntineoplastic(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the orderable is not a restricted antimicrobial (formulary restriction flag, governed content [HUMAN]; an unknown restriction flag on
     * an antimicrobial counts as restricted); or an indication is recorded and either an approver is recorded who holds the
     * antimicrobial-approval role of the stewardship policy and is not the signer (§10.3 C 'restricted antimicrobials need an indication
     * and an approver at order entry'; §21 row 3.1), or the order's priority is STAT or ASAP, in which case the approval follows as an
     * owned task (createAntimicrobialApprovalTask) so a time-critical first dose is never delayed (SI-12 time-critical list; DN-052 item
     * 16)
     */
    fun restrictedAntimicrobialApproved(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the orderable is not an antimicrobial (formulary class flag, governed content [HUMAN]; an unknown class flag on a medicine counts as
     * antimicrobial); or the order carries a stop date or a review date (§10.3 C 'every antimicrobial order carries a stop or review date')
     */
    fun antimicrobialStopOrReviewDateSet(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the order is not an antimicrobial (unknown class counts as antimicrobial), a PRN order or an imaging order; or an indication is
     * recorded (§9.5 'indication required for antimicrobials (with the stewardship control set), PRNs and imaging')
     */
    fun indicationRecordedWhereRequired(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the order's dose is not expressed per body weight or per body-surface area; or the patient has the one dosing weight of record that
     * SI-05 requires, measured, stated or estimated, recorded with its date and its source (§9.5 'no weight-based medicine signable without
     * a dated weight'; SI-05 clause a; CTRL-0005-3; R11 §15 item 3). An estimated weight with a date and source (for example in paediatric
     * resuscitation) counts. No staleness limit is encoded: any limit is governed content [HUMAN]. The weight is shown, never used in a
     * calculation
     */
    fun datedWeightRecordedIfWeightBased(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the draft replaces no order; or the order it replaces is in pending-verification, active or on-hold, no other signed order replaces
     * it yet, and that order's replacement Discontinue would pass its guard for this signer and this command (mayDiscontinueOrder holds for
     * the signer on that order). So revokeReplacedOrder can never fail once Sign's guard holds. DN-052 item 10
     */
    fun replacedOrderDiscontinuable(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /** the order's verification status is not returned (pending or verified; absent for a non-medication order) */
    fun notReturned(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /** the exact complement of notReturned: the verification status is returned (by Verify with a mismatch or by ReturnToPrescriber) */
    fun verificationReturned(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * either control set A does not apply to this order and no independently calculated dose has been recorded for it since its last
     * submission (Sign or Resubmit); or the latest independently calculated dose recorded since the last submission was recorded by the
     * verifying pharmacist, who attested that it matches the order, and it equals the ordered dose exactly in value and UCUM unit (every
     * bound of a dose range; §2.1 dose arithmetic clause b: exact comparison, no conversion). The ordered dose is the absolute dose amount
     * the prescriber entered on the order; the system never derives it from a per-weight or per-area basis (SI-05 clause c), so an order to
     * which control set A applies that carries no prescriber-entered absolute dose fails here (the pharmacist returns it). Control set A
     * applies while the Dose Engine is not active at the site (always in the MVP: reg-dose is P2) to every dose based on weight or
     * body-surface area at any age, every high-alert infusion (formulary high-alert flag and an infusion order) and every neonatal order
     * (the governed neonatal definition, content [HUMAN]); an unknown flag counts as applying
     */
    fun controlSetASatisfied(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * an independently calculated dose has been recorded for this order since its last submission (whether or not control set A applies),
     * and the latest one does not equal the ordered dose exactly in value and UCUM unit (a unit mismatch counts as a mismatch, §2.1 clause
     * b). Disjoint from controlSetASatisfied, which needs no recorded dose or an exactly equal one. Earlier calculations stay on record
     */
    fun controlSetAMismatch(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the pharmacist chose an intervention reason from the governed list (outcome codes, §9.10; content [HUMAN]), never defaulted (§6.5;
     * the channel adapter owns the 'chosen' mark)
     */
    fun returnReasonEntered(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the issuer recorded a response to the return: the order is confirmed as written, with a reason chosen by the issuer from the governed
     * list (content [HUMAN]), never defaulted, and the issuer is the ordering practitioner or a practitioner who satisfies
     * ordererPrivileged's licence and privilege conditions for this orderable, and is not the user who returned the order (the pharmacist
     * cannot clear their own return, DN-052 item 15; an unknown issuer or an unknown returning user fails). A change to the order is never
     * a response: it is a replacement (DraftReplacement)
     */
    fun prescriberResponseRecorded(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the issuer chose a hold reason, never defaulted (§6.5): a code from the governed list (content [HUMAN]; R11 §10.2 'held (e.g., NPO,
     * OR)'), or 'other' with free text, which is always offered so that a missing or incomplete list never blocks a hold; a registered
     * system principal gives the system reason it is registered for
     */
    fun holdReasonEntered(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the order is not a medication order, or its verification status is verified (it was verified before it was held: no Verify happens in
     * on-hold)
     */
    fun verifiedOrNotMedication(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /** the exact complement of verifiedOrNotMedication: a medication order whose verification status is pending or returned */
    fun medicationAwaitingVerification(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the clock reading in the facts is at or after the draft's next review time and no owner task for this review is open. The first
     * review time is the creation time plus the governed draft review interval (a shorter interval for a cutover pre-build); later ones
     * follow at the same interval. A missing interval uses the vendor default interval (governed content [HUMAN]), never zero.
     * Schedule-time comparison only
     */
    fun draftReviewDue(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the clock reading in the facts is at or after the hold's next review time (the hold time plus the governed hold review interval, or
     * the review time the issuer set on the hold if earlier) and no review task for this hold is open. A missing interval uses the vendor
     * default interval (governed content [HUMAN]), never zero
     */
    fun holdReviewDue(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the fulfilling module reports the order's fulfilment complete (its answer, R11 §7.3 fulfilment as tasks). For a medication order: its
     * stop date has passed (for a once-only or fixed-count order, the stop date is the due time of its last scheduled dose) and every dose
     * of the order is in a terminal administration state, none scheduled or in-progress (medication-administration.yaml). For a diagnostic
     * order: every requested item has a result in final, amended or corrected (result.yaml); a cancelled or entered-in-error result does
     * not complete the order, which is re-run or discontinued. For any other order: its fulfilment tasks are done. An unknown answer fails
     */
    fun fulfilmentComplete(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /** the discontinue reason is 'replaced', which only the signing of a replacing order sets; a user is never offered it */
    fun reasonIsReplacement(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /** the exact complement of reasonIsReplacement (including no reason at all) */
    fun reasonIsNotReplacement(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the issuer chose a discontinue reason, never defaulted (§6.5): a code from the governed list (content [HUMAN]), or 'other' with free
     * text, which is always offered so that a missing or incomplete list never blocks a stop; a registered system or interface principal
     * gives the system reason it is registered for (for example the patient's death). The list never contains 'replaced'
     */
    fun discontinueReasonEntered(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the replacing order named by the command carries a `replaces` link to this order and is signed by the same command (the same command
     * id: one atomic order-sign transaction, §9.5)
     */
    fun replacingOrderSignedTogether(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * the issuer holds the privilege that the governed configuration requires to mark an order entered in error (§9.26; a Trust Plane
     * answer), and the audit record of the correction can be written with the command (an audit outage refuses the command; it never runs
     * unaudited). B.3's name, required on every exit from a terminal state (WP-0.5 spec §1.2). The reason is errorReasonEntered's
     */
    fun privilegedAndAudited(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean

    /** the issuer chose an entered-in-error reason from the governed list (content [HUMAN]), never defaulted (§6.5) */
    fun errorReasonEntered(facts: OrderFacts): Boolean
}

